    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000054",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "**Spec point** — `spcpt_SQ9B87PZ4cMwszkM`",
    "reading_order" : 54,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "paragraph",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000055",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "Limitations of Standard Electrode Potential Predictions",
    "reading_order" : 55,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "heading",
    "heading_level" : 2,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000056",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "The **thermodynamic feasibility** of a reaction can be deduced from the electrode potential, however, it gives no information about the rate of reaction",
    "reading_order" : 56,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000057",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "As standard electrode potentials are measured using solutions, we have to consider the le Châtelier's effect on concentration using non-standard conditions",
    "reading_order" : 57,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000058",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "For example, the redox equilibrium equation and standard electrode potential for the V<sup>3+</sup> | V<sup>2+</sup> system are:",
    "reading_order" : 58,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000059",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "V<sup>3+</sup> (aq) + e<sup>-</sup> ⇌ V<sup>2+</sup> (aq)       *E*<sup>θ</sup> = +0.26 V",
    "reading_order" : 59,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "paragraph",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000060",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "If the concentration of V<sup>3+</sup> (aq) is greater than 1.0 mol dm<sup>-3</sup>, then the equilibrium will shift to the right",
    "reading_order" : 60,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000061",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "This will remove electrons from the system, therefore, making the electrode potential less negative",
    "reading_order" : 61,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000062",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "If the concentration of V<sup>2+</sup> (aq) is greater than 1.0 mol dm<sup>-3</sup>, then the equilibrium will shift to the left",
    "reading_order" : 62,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000063",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "This will add electrons to the system, therefore, making the electrode potential more negative",
    "reading_order" : 63,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000064",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "Any change to the concentration will cause a change to the electrode potential and, therefore, to the overall cell potential",
    "reading_order" : 64,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000065",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "This is true of any change to the conditions that results in non-standard conditions",
    "reading_order" : 65,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000066",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "Reaction kinetics can also affect the prediction",
    "reading_order" : 66,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000067",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "1. The rate of reaction may simply be so slow that it looks like the reaction isn't happening, when it is\n2. The reaction may have a high activation energy which inhibits the reaction, for example:",
    "reading_order" : 67,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "paragraph",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000068",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "Cu<sup>2+</sup> (aq) + 2e<sup>-</sup> ⇌ Cu (s)   *E*<sup>θ</sup> = 0.34 V",
    "reading_order" : 68,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "paragraph",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000069",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "2H<sup>+</sup> (aq) + 2e<sup>-</sup> ⇌ H<sub>2</sub> (g)   *E*<sup>θ</sup> = 0.00 V",
    "reading_order" : 69,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "paragraph",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000070",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "The reaction of Cu<sup>2+</sup> (aq) + H<sub>2</sub> (g) → Cu (s) + 2H<sup>+</sup> (aq) is thermodynamically feasible with an electromotive force of +0.34 V",
    "reading_order" : 70,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000071",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "However, this reaction does not occur as the activation energy is so high which means that the reactants are **kinetically stable**",
    "reading_order" : 71,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000072",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "Another, more basic limitation is the fact that many redox reactions are not aqueous",
    "reading_order" : 72,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  } ],
